      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C02"],
      "claim": "Biperiden, a lipophilic piperidine anticholinergic, crosses the BBB with brain/plasma ratios of 7-12; this strong positive CNS-penetrant example is structurally distant from the query's guanidine-azocane dication and very low logD, limiting its relevance.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is guanethidine, a dicationic guanidine-azocane with very low logD and full ionization at pH 7.4. The supplied positive CNS-penetrant analogues are monobasic lipophilic amines and do not transfer to this scaffold; the negative polar-amine record and known peripheral restriction of guanethidine support a fail.",
